Danny's source panel vs the index CSV, and the origin of the variable-annuity funds' fees (inline checks, 11 Nov 2026).
Files: Dropbox\P16_LeverageMKT\Data\source_intake\raw data\index_funds_preprocess_oct2026.csv (source panel, written at line 146 of
       Dropbox\P16_LeverageMKT\Code\5_fund_market_data_for_Matteo_v6_nonlev_etf.R) and Code\python\nonLev_funds_product_month_level_v2_patched.csv.

1. Row counts. Source panel 675,551 fund-months, 6,077 funds. Index CSV 579,632 fund-months, 5,532 funds. Every CSV row is in the source
   panel (no CSV-only rows); fees and family codes agree on all 579,632 common rows. Source-only rows: 95,919 (545 funds are never exported: 42,763 rows).
2. The filter (build script, about line 555):
   regDat=regDat[!is.na(product_mtna + product_L1_mtna + product_exp_ratio + product_fund_age + product_tracking_err + product_past_1yr_ret +
                        BLP_IV_hausman_exp_ratio + Conduct_IV_vw_ind_resid_1m)]
   and at export (line 831): product_mtna>0 & product_L1_mtna>0 & !is.na(product_exp_ratio).
3. The 95,919 source-only rows by first failing condition, in this order:
   no past 1-year return / tracking error (the fund's first 12 months)        38,713
   no expense ratio                                                           29,114
   assets missing or not positive                                              3,350
   lagged assets missing or not positive                                          80
   fund-level data complete, but the paper's Hausman IV is undefined
     (the family has no fund on another index that month)                     23,178
   index-month absent from the CSV (index-level conduct instrument missing)      426
   not explained by this reconstruction                                        1,058
4. Donors. 60,773 source-only rows have a fee and positive lagged assets, so they enter the paper's IV0 as donors (IV0 is built before the
   filter). That is 9.5% of all usable donor rows in the source panel. They are missing from any instrument rebuilt from the index CSV.
5. Fee imputation (build script, lines 89-99): fund5 = first five letters of the fund name, lower case. A missing expense ratio is filled
   forward within the fund, then by the mean fee of funds with the same fund5 on the same date, then by the mean over all dates of that fund5;
   after the merge it is filled backward and forward within the fund.
6. CRSP quarterly fund summary, Table 2 funds: share of records with a missing expense ratio: variable-annuity funds 0.968 (7,017 records),
   other funds 0.056 (80,575 records). Funds with no expense ratio in any CRSP record: 99 of the 112 variable-annuity funds, 1 of the 1,190 others.
   The 9 Allianz ("allia") variable-annuity funds have no CRSP expense ratio in any record.
